For follow-up: the win here relies on `<Combobox.Item>` children being referentially stable, and grouped items see no win (by default).

`Combobox.Collection` recreates children every keystroke. We can internalize it, but externally doing it already works:

```jsx
const ProduceItem = React.memo(function ProduceItem({ item }: { item: Produce }) {
  return (
    <Combobox.Item value={item}>
      <Combobox.ItemIndicator />
      <span>{item.label}</span>
    </Combobox.Item>
  );
});

<Combobox.Collection>
  {(item) => <ProduceItem key={item.id} item={item} />}
</Combobox.Collection>
```
